  "7511498261946552320": {
   "created": 1790880742,
   "author": "Robert Lee-Green",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/robert-lee-green-3013a349_thank-you-to-our-2026-partners-ideas-activity-7511498261946552320-xRe6",
   "text": "Proud to see Etched Tech amongst such a strong group of partners supporting Ideas Fest 2026.\n\nA huge thank you to the Ideas Fest team for bringing together such an ambitious community of founders, investors, entrepreneurs and innovators and for giving us the opportunity to be part of it.\n\nTo see Etched alongside names including TikTok, Goldman Sachs, Xero, Innovate UK Business Connect and UBS is a great milestone for us and a reflection of the company we\u2019re building. \n\nNot to mention having CMS UK and CMS equIP for Start-ups partner with us at the event. \n\nWe had some brilliant conversations throughout the event around the value of an idea, innovation and the importance of being able to evid",
   "disc_score": 7,
   "checks": {},
   "promoted": false,
   "miss": 0,
   "added": 1790891893
  },
  "7511554896702136320": {
   "created": 1790894245,
   "author": "Augustin Sayer",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/gussayer_climatetech-aiinfrastructure-deeptech-activity-7511554896702136320-taEs",
   "text": "In this week's Fault Lines Podcast, I received Matt Logan, GP and co-founder of Earthshot Ventures. These guys coined the term \"clean intelligence stack\" and this is their investment thesis. From critical mineras, to clean energy and efficient compute, their goal is to scale AI without derailing climate goals.\n\nAnd the track record speaks for itself. Investors in startups/scaleups such as Etched and KoBold Metals among many others!\n\nLink in comment!\n\n#climatetech #AIinfrastructure #deeptech",
   "disc_score": 2,
   "checks": {},
   "promoted": false,
   "miss": 0,
   "added": 1790896280
  },
  "7511621065484222464": {
   "created": 1790910021,
   "author": "Ambar Laad",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ambar-laad_the-ai-infrastructure-conversation-for-the-activity-7511621065484222464-JpFQ",
   "text": "The AI infrastructure conversation for the last two years has been about one thing: training. Nvidia GPUs, H100 clusters, data centres the size of small cities. Look at where the money actually went in Q3 2026. \n\nInference-focused chip startups pulled 67% of all disclosed AI chip funding. $3.62B across eight deals. Etched, which builds chips hardwired exclusively to run AI models at inference time, took $700M alone.\n\nThe capital doesn't agree with the narrative.\n\nTraining gets the headlines because it's where the biggest numbers live. But training a model happens once. Serving it happens billions of times, forever, at a cost structure that determines whether the whole business is profitable.",
   "disc_score": 8,
   "checks": {},
   "promoted": false,
   "miss": 0,
   "added": 1790925854
  },
  "7511632555088101376": {
   "created": 1790912760,
   "author": "Li Liu",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/li-liu-7ab700236_anthropic-is-going-public-at-a-2-trillion-activity-7511632555088101376-zFCx",
   "text": "anthropic is going public at a $2 trillion valuation. let that sit for a second\n\nThey're reportedly seeking $100B+ in IPO proceeds alone.\n\nNvidia just locked in a $7B licensing deal with Poolside, valuing the AI lab at $12B.\n\nPhysical AI funding hit $47.4B across 521 deals in just the first half of 2026.\n\nXPENG Robotics raised a $900M+ Series A at a $6.3B post-money valuation.\n\nEtched, the custom AI chip company, doubled its valuation to $21B.\n\nAlibaba raised $10.2B in a Hong Kong share placement to fund its AI infrastructure.\n\nLambda is seeking a $3B pre-IPO round and Groq raised $350M for its neocloud.\n\nGas-turbine backlogs are projected to stretch to 2031 because AI data centers are eatin",
   "disc_score": 1,
